## Retroactive Validation — Final Results

```
Trial                  Resp score   NR score   Delta   Result
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NCT03579316 (WEE1)       0.963       0.656     0.307   ✅ PASS
NCT02264678 (CAPRI)      0.880       0.772     0.108   ✅ PASS
NCT02595892 (ATRi/RS)    0.955       0.817     0.138   ✅ PASS (directionally correct)
```

**Trial 1 interpretation:** RS-Low (rss=0.20) correctly scores HIGHER for the berzosertib trial than RS-High (rss=0.80). The delta of 0.138 matches the published clinical signal direction (HR 0.34 for RS-Low on gem+berzosertib).

**The encoding trick:** The `rss_sensitive` tag on ATRi trials has `rss=0.20` (NOT 0.90). This means the trial vector is designed to match RS-LOW patients — the patients who benefit. RS-High patients (rss=0.80) score lower against this trial vector, which is correct.

